Subject: Cantor Procedure Tool Interoperability Gap Assessment

@ [assessment_uuid] cd206c14-752c-40e3-bdd4-bd06784b5529
@ [base_CLI] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Procedure_Tool_CLI.sop
@ [preparation] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Procedure_Tool_Preparation.sop
@ [query_MCP] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Read_Only_MCP_Adapter_Profile.sop

& [CurrentCapability] is executable and bounded
  + schema exposes the closed cantor.exchange operation vocabulary and semantic field contract
  + prepare constructs an exact run request from explicit candidate and lane parameters
  + run executes and independently verifies one fake effectless checkpoint outcome
  + verify independently checks a supplied outcome and returns exact digest bindings
  + all operations use bounded local JSON process I/O

& [DiscoverabilityGap] is concrete
  + no dedicated operator protocol document previously described the four operations together
  + prepare input contains nested public core forms whose complete field grammar is not shown by the semantic schema command
  + the Rust subprocess tests are executable truth but are not a convenient integration guide

& [MachineSchemaGap] is unresolved
  + ProviderNeutralToolSchema is Cantor semantic metadata and is not JSON Schema
  + procedure CLI request and response wrappers do not publish a provider-ready nested JSON Schema
  + core procedure forms do not currently derive a shared machine-schema representation
  + manually maintaining a second deep schema would risk drift from strict serde forms

& [MCPGap] is unresolved
  + current cantor-mcp exposes query_sop only
  + it is bound to a signed SOP runtime environment or resident service, not an authorship lane
  + adding cantor.exchange there would combine distinct startup, trust, size, and error contracts
  + no procedure MCP tool, resource, prompt, service backend, or provider controller is implemented

& [RecommendedDependencyOrder] is explicit
  + first specify a canonical schema derivation and compatibility contract for public procedure machine forms
  + then project prepare, run, and verify through a provider-neutral tool-definition record
  + then prove a fake MCP or function-tool controller against exact subprocess equivalence
  + only then select one real provider replay under separate live authority

& [RejectedShortcut] remains absent
  + do not label the semantic schema as JSON Schema
  + do not paste an unverified handwritten deep schema into provider configuration
  + do not add procedure operations to query_sop
  + do not modify llama.cpp before an ordinary external controller demonstrates a measured interface shortfall

& [Disposition] is current_protocol_documented_next_schema_frontier_unassigned
  + no behavior or implementation authority is granted by this assessment
